on-arrival: tak_dla_rozwoju_launched = 1; tak_rozwoj_party_name = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju"; news_headline = "Paulina Matysiak opens a cross-party campaign for major development projects"

= June 2024 — A railway map crosses the party line

Paulina Matysiak, a Razem MP known for rail and public-investment policy, has
launched Tak! Dla Rozwoju with Marcin Horała, the PiS MP who served as the
government's plenipotentiary for the Central Communication Port. They call it
a campaign for projects too large to fit one electoral term. Neither calls it
a new party.

Razem leader Adrian Zandberg sees a policy case and a political boundary. If
Matysiak may organise around development with a PiS partner, she can also ask
whether abortion, LGBT+ rights and secularism should define who is permitted
inside the Left. We must decide whether this becomes an internal current, a
bounded infrastructure campaign or a disciplinary offence.

- @tak_development_wing
- @tak_policy_campaign
- @tak_party_discipline

@tak_development_wing
title: Let Matysiak organise a developmental-conservative wing in Razem
subtitle: Give state-led development an organised caucus and permit cultural dissent; feminist and progressive organisers will contest the bargain.
on-arrival: matysiak_development_pressure += 24; razem_right_score += 16; left_right_score += 6; economic_issue_salience += 8; cultural_issue_salience -= 8; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience -= 6; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience -= 6; public_mood_pending_secular_state_salience -= 4; labor_credibility += 4; progressives_dissent += 7; feminist_trust -= 4; news_headline = "Razem permits a developmental wing to contest its cultural priorities"

Matysiak receives meetings, a programme conference and the right to organise
Razem members around rail, energy and large public investment. Her supporters
can now argue openly that an efficient developmental state matters more than
agreement on every cultural question.

Zandberg keeps the dispute inside the party and loses the ability to call it a
personal freelance. Labour organisers welcome the investment case; feminist
and LGBT+ allies see their claims turned from membership conditions into items
which a recognised faction may postpone.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the new Razem current on the events desk

@tak_policy_campaign
title: Keep Tak! Dla Rozwoju as a disciplined infrastructure campaign
subtitle: Permit cooperation project by project while Razem keeps its programme and whip; both founders must stay inside the fence.
on-arrival: matysiak_development_pressure += 10; economic_issue_salience += 4; labor_credibility += 3; local_network += 2; razem_cohesion += 2; tak_rozwoj_party_name = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju"; news_headline = "Tak! Dla Rozwoju remains a bounded policy campaign"

The association may publish project audits and convene local supporters, but
Matysiak accepts the Razem whip and no separate cultural platform. Horała gets
a partner on infrastructure, not a bridge into the party's internal life.

The boundary gives the campaign useful work and postpones the identity fight.
Every future joint appearance will now be judged against it, which means the
first breach will be clearer as well as more public.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the campaign boundary on the events desk

@tak_party_discipline
title: Open disciplinary proceedings over the cross-party association
subtitle: Reassert the party boundary through a formal hearing; turn Matysiak's project into a test of who may remain in Razem.
on-arrival: matysiak_development_pressure += 6; razem_cohesion += 4; razem_dissent += 5; party_unity -= 2; progressive_credibility += 2; news_headline = "Razem subjects Matysiak's development association to party discipline"

Matysiak is ordered to explain the association before party bodies and to
choose between its cross-party leadership and Razem discipline. Members who
feared a quiet ideological shift recover a rule they can recognise.

The hearing gives Tak! Dla Rozwoju the conflict its launch lacked. Horała can
present a railway campaign as the victim of partisan dogma, while Matysiak's
supporters begin organising around whether she is expelled rather than which
projects are built.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the disciplinary case on the events desk

